# Issue #3194 (greenfield flag day): every document content-key bundle
# declares its epoch's `contentKeyCommitment`, so an older client without it
# is refused with 400. Production needs the greenfield reset, and clients must
# clear local data. Remove these exact diagnostics as soon as main contains the
# new contract.
POST /auth/register added the new required request property `initialOrganizationMetadataContainer/metadataDocument/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment` (shared schema: `DocumentContentKeyBundleRequest`, also at `initialRosterProfileContainer/metadataDocument/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`, `initialSystemContainers/items/metadataDocument/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment` and 3 more)
POST /organizations added the new required request property `initialOrganizationMetadataContainer/metadataDocument/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment` (shared schema: `DocumentContentKeyBundleRequest`, also at `initialRosterProfileContainer/metadataDocument/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`, `initialSystemContainers/items/metadataDocument/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment` and 3 more)
POST /blobs/{blobId}/attachment-bindings added the new required request property `documentSync/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`
POST /containers/with-metadata-document added the new required request property `metadataDocument/contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`
POST /documents added the new required request property `contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`
POST /documents/{documentId}/link added the new required request property `contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`
POST /documents/{documentId}/sync added the new required request property `contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`
POST /documents/{documentId}/unlink added the new required request property `contentKeyBundle/contentKeyCommitment`
